; AdaptiveMultiStrategyEA - index account, default setting for the DEMO account (chapters 100, 103 and 104).
; Two sleeves on the whole balance (InpIxEquityOffset=0):
;   1 reversion (R2 / D7 / IBS, unchanged rules) on US500, US100, US30 and JP225, InpIxRevUnitVol=4
;   2 trend: hold US100 while its close is above the 200-day average (reviewed every 7 days), InpIxTrendUnitVol=8
; Why: on the broker's own data, February 2020 - November 2026 (3,000,000 JPY), this earned about +21% per year with a
;   maximum drawdown of 30% (2020 +15%, 2021 +27%, 2022 -5%, 2023 +14%, 2024 +38%, 2025 +22%, 2026 +42%; worst 12 months -15%).
;   The previous default (reversion only at 5) earned +16% per year with a 29% drawdown (2022 -12%, worst 12 months -19%).
;   Last 3 years, real ticks: +129% (drawdown 21%) against +102% (18%).
; The trend sleeve fills the days on which the reversion rules hold nothing. Over 40 years of index data it earned a modest
;   return of its own; it lost a little in 2000-2008. JP225 is the weakest part of the evidence (chapter 101).
; Larger: AMS_Sleeves_Index_Growth.set. Reversion only (the reference of the earlier tests): AMS_Sleeves_Index.set.
InpEntryMode=8
InpIxRevSymbols=US500,US100,US30,JP225
InpIxTrendSymbols=US100
InpIxRuleR2=true
InpIxRuleD7=true
InpIxRuleIBS=true
InpIxRevUnitVol=4.0
InpIxTrendUnitVol=8.0
InpIxTrendCheckDays=7
InpIxMaxLev=10.0
InpIxBand=0.25
InpIxSLVolMul=4.0
InpIxVolModel=1
InpIxVixFile=AMS_vix.csv
InpIxVixLowMult=0.5
InpIxVixHighMult=1.5
InpIxRuleWeights=1,2,4
InpIxSoGuard=0.9
InpIxFlatMinutes=0
InpIxFlatEdgeBp=0.0
InpIxDelayMin=5
InpIxMaxSpreadPct=0.05
InpMaxMarginUsePct=90.0
InpIxJointRound=false
InpIxJointEps=0.25
InpIxWarmStart=true
InpIxRegimeDays=1500
InpIxRegimeThr=1.0
InpIxRegimeRef=US500
InpIxDryRun=false
InpIxEquityOffset=0
